+#### HTTP budgets and unified memory search
+
+The HTTP server defaults to a 30,000 ms socket inactivity timeout. For a slower
+cold-start workload, set `--request-timeout-ms 120000` or
+`RUFLO_MCP_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS=120000` before starting the server. This is an
+inactivity timer, not an absolute elapsed-time deadline. A longer client-side
+budget does not override the server setting; configure both layers deliberately.
+
+An HTTP timeout, a disconnected POST, or the closure of its SSE session cancels
+that request's unified memory search cooperatively. Cancellation takes effect at
+asynchronous phase and namespace boundaries; it cannot preempt a synchronous
+SQLite/WASM operation already running. Other in-flight requests are independent.
+The default stdio and WebSocket request behavior is unchanged.
+
+`memory_search_unified` keeps `searchTime` as its legacy completion timestamp;
+use the additive `elapsedMs` for elapsed duration. `complete` is false when any
+namespace search fails, enumeration fails, or enumeration reaches its 100,000-row
+cap with more rows remaining. `namespaceErrors` contains at most ten diagnostics;
+`namespaceErrorCount` and `namespaceErrorsTruncated` disclose any additional
+failures. Enumeration failure preserves the legacy namespace fallback and reports
+`enumerationError`. Partial results keep `success: true` without a top-level
+`error`; if no namespace search succeeds, the response reports `success: false`.
+An empty successful namespace is not a failure.
+
